{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_testing_multi_node_spec_multinodespec", "label": "MultiNodeSpec", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Laesst N Cluster-Nodes in einem Test-Prozess laufen; jeder ist ein echtes ActorSystem, die Kommunikation laeuft ueber einen In-Process-Transport statt TCP. Fuer Cluster-Verhalten (Sharding-Rebalances, Singleton-Failover, Gossip-Konvergenz), zum Reproduzieren verteilter Bugs und fuer CI-freundliche Cluster-Tests ohne Docker und ohne Ports.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/testing/multi-node-spec.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_testing_multi_node_spec_optionen", "label": "MultiNodeSpecOptionsType", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "roles (ein Node pro Rolle, der String ist zugleich der ActorSystem-Name und muss eindeutig sein), seedRoles (Default: die erste Rolle), addresses, failureDetector, gossipIntervalMs (Default 100 ms statt 1 s in Produktion), awaitTimeoutMs (Default 10 s), logLevel (leiser NoopLogger) und downing. Der Konstruktor wirft bei Duplikaten oder leerer Liste.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/testing/multi-node-spec.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_testing_multi_node_spec_crash_leave", "label": "crash(role) und leave(role)", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "crash reisst den Transport eines Nodes abrupt weg \u2014 die Peers beobachten Unreachable, gossipen die Aenderung und loesen Downing plus Failover aus; leave fuehrt einen sauberen Cluster-Austritt durch.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/testing/multi-node-spec.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_testing_multi_node_spec_await_helfer", "label": "Die await*-Helfer", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "awaitMembers, awaitMemberStatus und Verwandte pollen, bis die Bedingung gilt, oder werfen nach awaitTimeoutMs \u2014 sie ersetzen fragile setTimeout-Schlafphasen.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/testing/multi-node-spec.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_testing_multi_node_spec_testprobe", "label": "TestProbe pro Node", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "MultiNodeSpec hat keine Probe-Factory \u2014 man konstruiert eine TestProbe gegen systemFor(role). Jede Probe ist an das ActorSystem eines Nodes gebunden, was beim Testen von Routing verifiziert, dass eine Nachricht auf dem erwarteten Node landet.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/testing/multi-node-spec.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_testing_multi_node_spec_keine_serialisierung", "label": "MultiNodeSpec serialisiert nicht", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "Nachrichten gehen zwischen Nodes per REFERENZ, serialisierungsabhaengige Bugs tauchen also nicht auf \u2014 und ParallelMultiNodeSpec schliesst die Luecke nur zur Haelfte, weil Structured Clone Payloads akzeptiert, die der Wire ablehnt. Fuer echte Abdeckung die Nachricht in einem Unit-Test durch JsonSerializer round-trippen oder einen Echt-Cluster-Integrationstest fahren.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/testing/multi-node-spec.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_testing_multi_node_spec_keine_netzwerkfehler", "label": "Keine echten Netzwerk-Fehlermodi", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "Der In-Memory-Transport ist zuverlaessig: Paketverlust, TCP-Keepalive und Congestion gelten hier nicht. Fuer Netzwerk-Fault-Tests Toxiproxy plus echte Docker-Setups.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/testing/multi-node-spec.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_testing_multi_node_spec_keine_thread_isolation", "label": "Keine Thread-Isolation", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "Alle Nodes teilen Event-Loop und Speicher des Test-Prozesses: ein echter OOM auf einem Node OOMt den Test. Fuer Isolation ParallelMultiNodeSpec, das jeden Node in einem eigenen Worker-Thread laufen laesst.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/testing/multi-node-spec.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_testing_multi_node_spec_parallelmultinodespec", "label": "ParallelMultiNodeSpec", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Die Worker-Thread-Variante fuer Tests, die echte Parallelitaet brauchen (nebenlaeufige Journal-Schreibvorgaenge, Scheduler-Interleaving). Zugleich eine der drei in CI quarantaenisierten Suites.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/testing/multi-node-spec.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_testing_multi_node_spec_multinodespec", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_testing_multi_node_spec_optionen", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/testing/multi-node-spec.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_testing_multi_node_spec_multinodespec", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_testing_multi_node_spec_crash_leave", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/testing/multi-node-spec.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_testing_multi_node_spec_multinodespec", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_testing_multi_node_spec_await_helfer", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/testing/multi-node-spec.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_testing_multi_node_spec_multinodespec", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_testing_multi_node_spec_testprobe", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/testing/multi-node-spec.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_testing_multi_node_spec_multinodespec", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_testing_multi_node_spec_keine_serialisierung", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/testing/multi-node-spec.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_testing_multi_node_spec_multinodespec", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_testing_multi_node_spec_keine_netzwerkfehler", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/testing/multi-node-spec.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_testing_multi_node_spec_keine_thread_isolation", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_testing_multi_node_spec_parallelmultinodespec", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/testing/multi-node-spec.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_testing_multi_node_spec_multinodespec", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_reference_glossary_gossip", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/testing/multi-node-spec.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_t